s: the importance of cascade analysis in describing, counting, and preventing medical errors. Ann Fam Med. 2004 Jul&#x02013;Aug;2(4):292&#x02013;93 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15335125</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greenfield</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaplan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ware</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Expanding patient involvement in care. Effects on patient outcomes</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>1985</year><volume>102</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>520</fpage><lpage>528</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Greenfield S, Kaplan S, Ware, JE, Jr. Expanding patient involvement in care. Effects on patient outcomes. Ann Intern Med. 1985 Apr;102(4): 520&#x02013;28. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3977198</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hulka</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Cassel</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kupper</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Burdette</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Communication, compliance, and concordance between physicians and patients with prescribed medications</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</source><year>1976</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>847</fpage><lpage>853</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hulka BS, Cassel JC, Kupper LL, Burdette JA. Communication, compliance, and concordance between physicians and patients with prescribed medications. Am J Public Health. 1976;66:847&#x02013;53. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">961952</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><c